record(s,t,rs,decs,inv,'A large opening draft, surrounded by a brown boundary and crossed diagonally, discusses a spectral sequence and torsion groups. The surviving paragraph gives sequence (5.1), describes the divisor sheaf and states a connecting-map assertion modulo torsion. The raised condition about X, including noethérien, sits below the cancelled block and belongs to this surviving paragraph. The closing lines introduce an isomorphism of étale sheaves and end with a colon. The slanted instruction reads “donner le corollaire 5.4.”; the sheet numbered 175 (scan 176) calls its 5.4 a proposition. Both labels are retained.\n\n179.N1: The direct-image reading i_* uses the author’s repeated R^q i_*(G_m) and the lower definition R*_X=i_*(G_mx/y). The subscript star is drawn as a compact crossed mark; the direct-image notation supplies the reading of this recurring shape. This is a notation/background use, not a proof of the spectral-sequence or torsion claims. The lower G subscript remains uncertain under the diagonal stroke. The clearer Div in (5.1) gives the notation comparison for scan 176. No external reference was consulted. Archive number 178; no date.',doubts=[['179','inner cancellation after Or',r'\unsure{comme les}','short letters hidden by strike','low'],['179','inner cancellation after on trouve que',r"\unsure{l’on a} \unsure{dans|sur} les \unsure{les} groupes",'several short letters remain hidden; repeated les preserved','low'],['179','old operator in R*_X definition',r'\deleted{\unsure{Ri_*}}','overwritten operator','low'],['179','G subscript in that definition',r'\unsure{x|y}','diagonal passes through small subscript','low'],['179','raised topology phrase ending',r'\unsure{)}','closing parenthesis / curved insertion stroke','low'],['179','overwritten coefficient in target',r'\deleted{\unsure{R|D}}','older letter behind G','low'],['179','cancellation after torsion',r'\unsure{pour i|si}','long low run with final dot','low'],['179','last long cancellation opening',r'\unsure{on aura|ne sera pas}','letters partly hidden by strike','low']],notation=[['Higher direct-image subscript',r'R^qi_*','179','Compact crossed star in the spectral-sequence term and repeated sheaf term.'],['Divisor sheaf',r'\uline{\mathrm{Div}}_X','179','D, dotted short i and looped v; all three occurrences are underlined.']],hand=['The v of Div curls upward and can resemble a small oval; the dotted i is compressed close to D. The clear occurrence in (5.1) supplies a comparison for scan 176.','A large cancellation boundary can pass close to later interlinear additions. Here the si X est condition and noethérien lie below the lower boundary; H includes the condition in the struck draft and omits noethérien.','The slanted donner le has a tall d loop followed by a nearly level onner run; the crop separates this from H’s Démonstration du.'],abbreviations=[['top','topologie'],['mod','modulo'],['pt','point']],events=[['179.N1','carried as background without fault found','Used direct-image notation to read the compact crossed star beneath i; no proof of the page’s spectral-sequence or torsion statements.']],extra='Additional certainty-only inspections: the early crossed i subscript is read as * on crop 179 (1178,350,1229,418), with the repeated notation recorded above; the last cancelled l’isomorphisme resolves on 179 (931,1988,1264,2051). The short cancelled des and the clear final qu’on a un are settled in the native half. H’s trailing editorial note about a different, otherwise blank leaf and its end-document command supply no source text for this scan. All crop boxes are recorded above or in the corresponding rows.')
